    "id": "x4_linear_difference_projection_codegree_bound",
    "title": "Linear-difference translated-divisor projection codegree bound",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For a fixed base support and side width e, every fixed added-locator or removed-locator projection fiber of the d=1 translated complementary-divisor incidence has Johnson codegree at most v(e-1)/(e^2-v), where v is the corresponding side universe and e^2>v. The exact official corridor implies t_XR>=2^31; since d=1 forces e>=t_XR+2 and N=2^41, both projection codegrees are at most 1024. This bounds multiplicity over a projection but does not bound the projection population or the total d=1 stratum.",
